<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alessandro Farnese, Duke of Parma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1545">1545</a>–<a href="/years/1592">1592</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-iii">Alessandro Farnese</a>, Duke of Parma, was the most famous general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>. As governor of the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> from 1578, he reconquered the southern provinces through diplomacy and siege, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a> in 1585. He was due to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1588. He succeeded his father as duke of Parma and Piacenza in 1586.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alessandro-farnese-duke-of-parma.jpg" alt="Alessandro Farnese, Duke of Parma" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otto van Veen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vaenius_-_Alexander_Farnese.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under the Habsburgs Brabant became a main theatre of the Eighty Years' War, with the Spanish Fury at Antwerp in 1576, <b>Alexander Farnese</b>'s siege of Antwerp in 1584–1585, and in 1706 the Duke of Marlborough's victory at the Battle of Ramillies gave the allies control of the duchy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-brabant">Duchy of Brabant · Military</a></li></ul></section>
